[C2C] STATE FINDINGS · ROUND 26
Medium — game/src/core/realm/body/BodyProgressionSystem.physique.test.ts — the new test proves the two underlying functions independently, but not the actual restore/preflight path required by the ruling. The test manually calls applyAllBodyModifiers(player) and then manually calls assertBodyProgressionIntegrity(player). That establishes that rebuild does not auto-heal and that integrity rejects the torn state, but it does not prove the real save-restore entry point invokes that integrity check before accepting the save. The Round-22 resolution explicitly pins restore behavior: behind-grade persisted state must be rejected at restore preflight. Add/retain a test through the actual restore/session-load API showing (a) completed chapter + persisted advanced physiqueGrade restores unchanged and (b) completed chapter + behind grade is rejected without mutation. Without that integration pin, a future restore call-site regression could bypass the invariant while this test remains green.
The production-side restore contract itself is now correctly documented and structurally separated: applyPhysiqueAdvancement() remains live-completion-only, applyAllBodyModifiers() does not invoke it, and persisted physiqueGrade remains the authority rather than being re-derived during rebuild.
The chapter-kind finding is resolved for the currently authored registry. EXPECTED_BODY_CHAPTER_KIND explicitly pins body_refinement -> refinement and meridian -> meridian, and validator tests reject valid-vocabulary but wrong per-ID classifications. No name-substring inference is involved. Future IDs remain deliberately unpinned until authored, which is consistent with the stated extension seam.
[C2C] END
